                             sending specially crafted packets, it              
                             is able to execute arbitrary code on               
                             the target machine, allowing full                  
                             access. This is typically the first                
                             step in a multi-layered attack                     
                             strategy that includes deploying                   
                             ransomware or other malicious                      
                             payloads.                                          
                                     After the leak, EternalBlue                
                             was used to launch extensive                       
                             cyberattacks, including the infamous               
                             WannaCry ransomware attack in May                  
                             2017. This attack affected over                    
                             200,000 computers across 150                       
                             countries, with total damages ranging              
                             into the billions of dollars. The                  
                             exploit's ability to spread within                 
                             networks without user interaction                  
                             makes it particularly dangerous and                
                             effective as a tool for rapid                      
                             dissemination of malware.                          
                                     Despite patches being released             
                             by Microsoft, many unpatched systems               
                             are still vulnerable to EternalBlue,               
                             and it remains in use by                           
                             cybercriminals. The legacy of                      
                             EternalBlue highlights the importance              
                             of regular system updates and the                  
                             potential dangers of stockpiling cyber             
                             weapons.                                           
